# .env.example — the template for $HERMES_HOME/.env
#
# COPY THIS, DO NOT EDIT IT IN PLACE. The real file lives on the machine, never here:
#
#   Windows:  %LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes\.env
#   else:     ~/.hermes/.env      then  chmod 600 ~/.hermes/.env
#
# NO KEY EVER GOES IN configs/hermes/config.yaml. Every remote provider there declares
# `key_env: <NAME>` and holds no value; Hermes resolves the name against this file at
# runtime. That separation is the design, and .gitignore now enforces the repo half of
# it -- until 2026-09-23 it protected python bytecode and nothing else, so a .env
# dropped in the repo root would have been committed silently.
#
# Values below are shown as their PREFIX ONLY, so the shape is recognisable and no
# credential is written down.

# --- required: the two cloud tiers -------------------------------------------
# NO HF_TOKEN ANYMORE. DeepSeek is fully removed from this build (2026-09-28, on
# request, repo-wide), parent included -- parent moved to custom:local (the
# `local` block below), not to another cloud provider. The `hf-router` provider
# it lived on is removed entirely, since nothing else in this file ever used it.

# Subagent tier + fallback 1 + MoA reference model + vision.
# custom:nvidia-nim -> nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning
# (swapped 2026-09-27: the prior id, llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1.5 -- itself
# swapped from nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b 2026-09-25 -- is confirmed dead, HTTP 410,
# EOL 2026-08-26)
# Get one at https://build.nvidia.com -> "Get API Key"
NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...

# 429 fallback AND two heavy auxiliary slots (compression, web_extract).
# custom:or-fallback -> qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b (reverted off DeepSeek 2026-09-28)
# compression REWRITES CONVERSATION HISTORY, so this one is not optional in practice:
# without it that slot falls back to the parent and silently costs parent-tier tokens.
# Get one at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# --- no key needed, but no longer optional: the local tier --------------------
# custom:local    Ollama    http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#
# THIS IS THE PARENT NOW (moved off DeepSeek/hf-router 2026-09-28, on request:
# "the current parent is the 49B Nemotron"). Ollama being unreachable, or the
# 49B GGUF not actually pulled, means Hermes has no parent at all -- not a
# degraded tier the way it was when this section was written. Needs BOTH
# models pulled: the 3.4 GB floor model and the ~58.68 GB 49B parent/aggregator
# GGUF (split file) -- see the `local` provider's comment in config.yaml for
# both `ollama pull` commands.
#
# `custom:local-vl` (llama.cpp, :8080) used to be listed here too -- retired
# 2026-09-25 along with hermes3:8b, on request. `vision` routes to the cloud
# now (nvidia-nim); there is only the one local PROVIDER left, serving two
# models.
#
# Loopback and takes NO key. config.yaml gives it the literal placeholder
# `api_key: "no-key-required"` rather than a key_env, on purpose: an OpenAI-compatible
# client insists on sending an Authorization header, and a real key sent to a local
# server can land in that server's request log for no benefit.

# --- optional: web search ---------------------------------------------------
# SearXNG is the configured backend. Run it locally:
#   docker run -d -p 8888:8080 --name searxng searxng/searxng
SEARXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888

# WATCH THIS ONE. If FIRECRAWL_API_KEY is present in the environment it SILENTLY WINS
# over SearXNG, and you get billed for searches you thought were local. Leave it unset
# unless you mean it.
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...

# --- optional: Codex -------------------------------------------------------
# Codex is delegated to as a SUBPROCESS, not as an inference provider -- `openai-codex`
# stays in excluded_providers because Hermes' own provider and the Codex CLI read
# different token files against the SAME ChatGPT 5-hour window, which makes that
# window's spend invisible to itself.
#
# Prefer `codex login` (ChatGPT plan, no separate billing). Set this ONLY for metered
# per-token use.
# CODEX_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- not keys: paths the config resolves by name ----------------------------
# These are set as USER environment variables, not here -- the Hermes supervisor reads
# them to launch local MCP subprocesses. Listed so the full set is in one place.
#   HERMES_SKILLS_SERVER     full path to skills-mcp-server\dist\index.js
#   HERMES_COUNCIL_LAUNCHER  full path to scripts\hermes-council-launch.cmd
#   HERMES_COUNCIL_PYTHON    the interpreter that HAS hermes_council installed
#   HERMES_CODEX_LAUNCHER    full path to scripts\codex-mcp-launch.cmd
#   HERMES_CODEX_NODE        the node.exe the Codex shim should pin
#
# NOT HERMES_VENV_PYTHON. Pointing at the venv was the bug behind this build's
# ModuleNotFoundError: the supervisor substitutes its own runtime for a bare
# `command:` entry, so the import ran where the packages were not. The launcher is
# indirection the supervisor cannot reach through.
